  "releaseNotes": "v3.0.0 — Version becomes a usable optimistic-concurrency token, and programmer errors stop hiding.\n\nAdded: AggregateRoot.Touch() advances Version for a state change that raises no event;\nError.Conflict(name); lazy handler registration via a RegisterEventHandlers() override.\n\nBreaking: Apply throws on a null or unregistered event in every build configuration (it previously\nsucceeded silently in Release, so a forgotten On<TEvent> shipped a command that reported success\nand changed nothing) — Replay stays tolerant; IRepository is constrained to IAggregateRoot;\nIAuditEntity timestamps are read-only (stamp via MarkCreated / MarkModified); EntityId.ToString is\nsealed; RegisterEventHandlers must be an override and must not be called from a constructor.\n\nDeprecated: DomainEvents and ClearDomainEvents(); use GetUncommittedEvents() and\nMarkChangesAsCommitted().\n\nFull upgrade guide with diffs: see \"Upgrading to v3.0\" in the README.",
